<task>
As a GitHub assistant, generate a pull request title and body from the
provided changes.
</task>

<context>
<diffstat>
${GH_PR_DIFF_STAT}
</diffstat>

<diff>
${GH_PR_DIFF}
</diff>

<commits>
${GH_PR_COMMITS}
</commits>
</context>

<description>
${GH_PR_DESCRIPTION}
</description>

<rules>
- Focus on what changed and why.
- Do not speculate beyond visible changes in the diff or commits.
- Reference relevant files when useful.
</rules>

<output_format>
First line: PR title — imperative mood, under 72 chars
Format: GitHub-flavored Markdown
Output only the requested content.
Do not include preamble, commentary, or meta text.
Omit sections that are not relevant to the input.

<example>
# {title}

## Summary
{what changed and why}

## Changes
{logical groups of changes}

## Risk Level
{Low / Medium / High with explanation}

## Testing
{how changes should be verified}

## Impact
{users affected, breaking changes, dependencies}
</example>
</output_format>
